<task id="230a" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H13's checks fit the dedicated stamp: I3 checks the partition keys the stamp template declares, no shared-platform assumption or wording remains, naming/I1 inputs ship with the Worker, dead shell-out options go</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T230 part 1 (G5)</phase>
    <gate>after 229 (✅)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>H13 probe code + options + tests; acceptance-gate semantics.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Acceptance-gate correctness: a wrong probe either blocks every stamp or passes a broken one.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>L2 Core/Tests and the Worker csproj only.</parallel-reason>
    <tags>provisioning, provisioning-handler, l2-controlplane, model1-dedicated, tenant-isolation, testing</tags>
    <deps>229</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Audit and fix every H13 check that assumes a shared platform or would mis-judge a dedicated customer stamp.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 control plane, ARM SDK probes).</role>

  <goal>
    On a correctly provisioned dedicated stamp (Model 1 or Model 2) every H13 structural check passes, and on a broken one
    it fails for the real reason. No H13 check, message or option refers to a shared platform, a shared vault pattern or
    a Model 1 shared tier.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Mapped 2026-10-06 (SESSION 40 exploration):
      - I3 `CosmosPartitionKeyInvariantProbe` asserts every container's partition key is `/customerId`
        (ExpectedPartitionKeyPath, :93, compared :235-240), but the stamp's containers (infrastructure/bicep/modules/
        cosmos-db.bicep :96,127,159,205,239,279,310) use `/tenantId`, `/partitionKey`, `/subjectId` — so I3 would fail
        every real stamp; its unit test treats `/tenantId` as a violation. On a dedicated stamp the account itself is the
        customer boundary (one customer per Cosmos account); what can drift is a container deployed without the key the
        template declares.
      - Stale shared-platform wording: I2 `AiSearchTenantFilterInvariantProbe` :359-360 ("shared platform is
        under-provisioned (Model 1)"), T2 `DataverseAppUserPairT2Probe` :145, T3 `GraphAppRoleParityT3Probe` :259.
      - `NamingConformanceChecker` vault rule `^sprk-[a-z0-9]+-kv$` (:98-99) is the old shared-vault pattern (stamp vault =
        `sprk-{customerId}-{env}-kv`, customer.bicep keyVaultName); it and the I1 verifier read repo files
        (appsettings.template.json, Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1, environments.json, infrastructure/bicep, scripts/) that the
        Worker csproj may not copy to its publish output (Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1 zips the publish folder) — verify what
        each reads at runtime and what happens when it is absent.
      - `H13AcceptanceOptions` :33-71 still carries shell-out settings (PwshExecutable, AzCliExecutable, script paths,
        timeouts) from the retired az/pwsh implementations.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/** (I1–I5 probes, T1–T7 probes, NamingConformanceChecker, H13AcceptanceOptions, E2EAcceptanceModule)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Worker/*.csproj; scripts/provisioning/Deploy-ControlPlane.ps1</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/cosmos-db.bicep; infrastructure/bicep/customer.bicep (keyVaultName)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Handlers/*Probe*Tests.cs, NamingConformanceCheckerTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="I3">I3 compares each deployed container with the partition key `cosmos-db.bicep` declares for it (a parity test reads the bicep so the two cannot drift); a container missing its declared key, with a different key, or a declared container that is absent → Failed; ARM/RBAC trouble stays InfraFault.</constraint>
    <constraint source="needed-or-remove">Options and inputs nothing reads go; an input a check needs at runtime must ship with the Worker (csproj content) or the check must not depend on it — no check may silently pass because its input is missing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="tests">ArmSdkTestFakes / hand-written fakes; never Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">I3: declared-key table + bicep parity test; probe + tests.</step>
    <step order="2">Wording: I2, T2, T3 and any other H13 text naming a shared platform / Model 1 shared tier.</step>
    <step order="3">Naming checker + I1: stamp vault pattern; establish what files each reads at runtime; ship them with the Worker or drop the dependency; fail closed when absent; tests.</step>
    <step order="4">Remove dead H13 shell-out options (and config/bicep app settings that set them).</step>
    <step order="5">Verify (ControlPlane tests, ArchTests, Worker 0 warnings, Worker publish contains what the checks read); Step 9.5; close.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">I3 passes a fake account whose containers carry exactly cosmos-db.bicep's keys and fails one with a missing/different key or a missing declared container; the probe's table equals the bicep's declarations (parity test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`git grep -i "shared platform\|shared-platform\|Model 1 shared\|Model1Shared"` finds nothing live in Handlers/E2EAcceptance (history comments marked as such excepted).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The naming checker accepts `sprk-{customerId}-{env}-kv` and every input it and I1 read is in the Worker publish output, or the check fails closed without it (test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No H13 option remains that nothing reads.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ControlPlane.Tests and ArchTests pass; Worker builds with 0 warnings.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A check turns out to need a live call to establish what the deployed shape is (ask before any live action).</trigger>
    <trigger>The I3 invariant's spec meaning (FR-30 "/customerId predicate") conflicts with the dedicated-stamp reading — surface per CLAUDE.md §6.5 if a spec/ADR change is needed.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <notes>
    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (SESSION 40).
    - I3: CosmosPartitionKeyInvariantProbe compares the stamp's account with cosmos-db.bicep — DeclaredPartitionKeys (7
      containers, /tenantId, /partitionKey, /subjectId) + DeclaredDatabaseName spaarke-ai, bicep parity test (non-empty
      literal names). Failed: a declared container with another/hierarchical/no key, or ANY container with no key.
      Membership drift (declared container absent / extra keyed container) is logged, not failed — the Worker table and the
      template H2a deploys ship on different schedules and ARM never deletes a retired container (code-review F3). It
      used to demand /customerId everywhere (FR-30 reserves that for L2's ProvisioningRun) → would have failed every stamp.
    - Wording: I2 (no "shared platform"), T2/T3 (tenantId is intake-required for every model); stale comments in
      H13RejectionCodes, IRegistrySetupStatusUpdater, IE2EValidationRunner, E2EValidationRunner, CompositeTrapVerifier, I2.
    - DEVIATION from AC3 ("ship the inputs or fail closed"), chosen by necessity (constraint "needed-or-remove", step 3 "or
      drop the dependency"): H13's naming check and runtime I1 probe both scanned REPOSITORY files that are identical for
      every run and absent from the Worker host (DOTNETCORE|10.0; publish has no scripts/ or infrastructure/), so each
      would have blocked every stamp (naming → QuarantineRequired, I1 → Resumable forever). Both removed (sub-agent):
      NamingConformanceChecker + seam + gate + codes + option; PackagedScriptTenantLiteral probe/verifier, InvariantKind.I1,
      InvariantI1Failed, ProvisioningScriptsDirectory; unregistered Placeholder*Verifier; unread shell-out options. H13
      runtime set = I2–I5 (CompositeInvariantVerifier now built from the enum — a new kind without a probe defers, never
      passes). I1 stays enforced by I1_NoHardcodedTenantTests (Tier-1, blocking). Naming conformance → NEW merge-blocking
      job in ci-tier1-blocking.yml (self-test + scan; the Router's required check — sdap-ci.yml is not required and its
      code-quality job is continue-on-error, so the first attempt there could never block: adr-check V1 / code-review F2).
      Vault rule R3 now accepts sprk-{customerId}-{env}-kv but not reserved ids / env tokens in that slot, case-sensitive,
      ≤ 24 chars (code-review F1); self-test fixtures added; Seed-ProductionKeyVault.ps1's drift default
      sprk-platform-prod-kv removed (VaultName mandatory; the script is inactive until a real prod exists). Spec FR-18 /
      FR-35 / SC #17 + asset rows, design rows, naming standard R3 + Enforcement, guide H13 row (pure C#) / §7.10 / §8 /
      §13.6 / gates list (God-class ratchet marked retired), constraints, skill, CHANGELOG.
    - Found and filed: G38 / T253 — H4b (pwsh Configure script) and H6 (pac org settings, pac required apps) still shell out
      on the Worker host that has neither tool → both fail live; queued before T186.
    - Step 9.5: code-review F1/F2 (Critical) fixed, F3 fixed (membership drift), F4 partly (non-empty-name check; hierarchical
      keys would already fail the parity test), F5 noted (no lease containers exist), F6/F7/F8 fixed, F9 accepted (retired
      DotnetR3GateVerifier, unregistered), F10 accepted (skipped-check name changed to naming-conformance-enforced-in-ci),
      F11 covered. adr-check V1 fixed; W1 recorded here; W2/W3/W6 fixed; W4 checked (sprk-xxxxxxxx-staging-kv = 24);
      W5 (deploy-bff-api.yml keeps its own advisory naming step feeding R3GateStatus) accepted; W7/W8 informational.
    - Observation: tests/scripts/Auth-V4-Operator-Script-Gates.Tests.ps1 fails 27/27 locally under Pester 6.2 at HEAD too
      (Set-A38cAzShadow not recognized) — pre-existing, not run in CI.
    - Tests: ControlPlane 2146 / 0 failed (1 skip); ArchTests 831/831; Worker/Api/Tests 0 warnings; naming lint 0 violations,
      self-test PASSED; workflow YAML parses.
  </notes>
</task>
